---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, OWNER } from '../site';
---

<LegalPage
  locale="en"
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What vedad-dizdarevic.dev does with your data: hosting, the contact form, spam protection and cookieless statistics."
>
  <p>
    Last updated: November 9, 2026. This is a translation for convenience. The{' '}
    <a href="/de/datenschutz/">German version</a> applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {OWNER}
    <br />
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
  </p>
  <p>I am not required to appoint a data protection officer and have not done so.</p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This site sets no cookies and shows no advertising.</li>
    <li>Reading it needs no account, and fonts come from this site, not from a third party.</li>
    <li>If you use the contact form, I use your details only to reply.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hosting and delivery</h2>
  <p>
    Every request passes through Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA,
    which provides DNS, encryption, caching, protection against attacks and the program that serves
    the pages. The pages themselves are stored at Amazon Web Services EMEA SARL, 38 Avenue John F.
    Kennedy, L-1855 Luxembourg, in the Frankfurt region.
  </p>
  <p>
    To deliver a page, Cloudflare processes your IP address, the time, the address requested, and
    your browser's technical details. Cloudflare's systems keep technical logs for a limited time.
    The legal basis is my legitimate interest in delivering this site securely and reliably (Art.
    6(1)(f) GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>Contact form and email</h2>
  <p>
    The form asks for your name, your email address, what your message is about, and the message. A
    function at Amazon Web Services in Frankfurt sends them to me by email through Amazon SES. My
    mailbox is hosted by{' '}
    <a href="https://purelymail.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Purelymail<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
    </a>
    , a service of Add Rabbit LLC, 502 W 7th St, Suite 100, Erie, PA 16502, USA, which receives the
    same information if you write to me directly.
  </p>
  <p>
    I use this information only to reply, and I do not pass it on for any other purpose. The
    function's logs contain neither your name, your address nor your message, and are deleted after
    30 days. I delete messages when they are no longer needed, unless a legal duty requires me to
    keep them.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is steps towards a possible contract at your request (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR), and
    otherwise my legitimate interest in answering your enquiry (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>Spam protection (Cloudflare Turnstile)</h2>
  <p>
    The form is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile. It loads only once you start on the form. It then
    runs checks in your browser to tell people from automated programs, and sends Cloudflare
    technical data such as your IP address and browser details. It does not read what you type.
    Details are in the{' '}
    <a
      href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Turnstile Privacy Addendum<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
    </a>
    .
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is my legitimate interest in keeping the form free of spam and abuse (Art.
    6(1)(f) GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>Statistics (Cloudflare Web Analytics)</h2>
  <p>
    A script from Cloudflare measures page views and loading times. It sets no cookies and does not
    follow you from site to site. I see only totals, such as how often a page was viewed. Your IP
    address reaches Cloudflare when the script loads and reports.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is my legitimate interest in knowing whether the site is used and works well
    (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    If you choose a light or dark theme, your choice is kept in your browser's local storage under{' '}
    <code>theme</code>. The home page also keeps <code>hero-arch</code> in session storage until you
    close the tab, so its illustration differs on your next visit. Neither leaves your browser. They
    serve only the display you see or asked for (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG).
  </p>

  <h2>Transfers outside the EU</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare is a US company, so data may be processed in the USA. Cloudflare is certified under
    the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, and data processing agreements with standard contractual
    clauses also apply.
  </p>
  <p>
    Purelymail's mail servers are at Amazon Web Services in Northern Virginia, USA. Any message you
    send me, through the form or directly, is stored there.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to other sites such as GitHub and LinkedIn. They process your data under their
    own policies once you open them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access your data and to have it corrected or deleted, to restrict its
    processing, and to receive it in a portable format (Art. 15 to 20 GDPR).{' '}
    <strong>
      Where I rely on legitimate interest, you may object at any time for reasons arising from your
      situation (Art. 21 GDPR).
    </strong>{' '}
    To do any of this, write to the address above.
  </p>
  <p>
    You may also complain to a data protection authority. Mine is the{' '}
    <a href="https://datenschutz.hessen.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Hessian Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information
      <span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <h2>Do you have to provide data?</h2>
  <p>
    No. Without the form's details I cannot reply through it, but you can always write to me by
    email instead.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
